#: ../../technical/articles/006-local-runtime-transport-worker-custody-and-lifecycle.md:12
msgid ""
"This chunk covers 17 local-runtime modules and 5,475 assigned source "
"lines (46,102 measured proxy tokens). I read every line across the "
"reader’s nine bounded pages. The files implement Windows and POSIX IPC, "
"transport hosting, per-profile workers, operation settlement and profile "
"mutations, native service-manager integration, and installed-client "
"admission. Static-only review: I did not launch a runtime, worker, "
"manager command, or native OS API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/006-local-runtime-transport-worker-custody-and-lifecycle.md:14
msgid "Capabilities and flow"
msgstr "Képességek és folyamat"

#: ../../technical/articles/006-local-runtime-transport-worker-custody-and-lifecycle.md:16
msgid ""
"An installed frontend first connects to the endpoint for the physical "
"storage root. `RuntimeLaunchDoor` attempts the verified connection before"
" asking the manager to start anything; it only starts a manager service "
"whose existing configuration is available and exactly bound. It does not "
"enable autostart, launch an uncontained process, or authenticate a "
"profile. A credential-reference admission path opens that client first, "
"then resolves the reference against the current installation/profile "
"binding and proves the API key over the verified connection; failure "
"closes only that new client. The status probe is passive: it connects and"
" asks whether the existing runtime is accepting, without invoking manager"
" control (startup.py (`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/startup.py`), "
"startup.py (`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/startup.py`), "
"runtime_client.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/runtime_client.py`), "
"runtime_credentials.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/runtime_credentials.py`), "
"management_status.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/management_status.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/006-local-runtime-transport-worker-custody-and-lifecycle.md:18
msgid ""
"The native endpoints bind the service name to owner and storage identity."
" POSIX resolves an existing owner-owned root to device/inode identity, "
"creates an owner-only socket namespace, and holds a persistent locked "
"inode before recovering a stale socket. A client checks the socket’s "
"owner/type and inode before and after connecting; peer credentials come "
"from the connected socket, not the pathname. Linux login capture "
"additionally obtains a live non-inheritable peer pidfd and binds the "
"session observation to it. The PIDFD socket option uses a known ABI "
"fallback only on listed architectures and otherwise refuses containment. "
"Windows uses a first-instance named pipe with a restrictive owner SID "
"ACL, rejects remote clients, opens narrow pipe rights, and checks the "
"kernel-reported peer process, token SID, liveness, and optional exact "
"image path while retaining the process handle. Both channels bound "
"reads/writes and apply deadlines to fragmented I/O (posix.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/posix.py`), posix.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/posix.py`), posix.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/posix.py`), windows.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/windows.py`), windows.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/windows.py`), windows.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/windows.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/006-local-runtime-transport-worker-custody-and-lifecycle.md:20
msgid ""
"`RuntimeTransportServer` owns one listener and a bounded pool of 32 "
"connection workers. It performs the runtime handshake, creates a "
"connection context from the verified peer, exposes status and owner-stop "
"control, and routes profile admission, enrollment, access-management, and"
" operation messages to the application profile handler. Per-connection "
"refusal ends that connection; unexpected failures fence the server. "
"Shutdown drains profile work, waits for accepted transports, and retains "
"listener ownership if cleanup is incomplete so a retry can finish the "
"drain. The server accepts a stop preview/confirmation only before that "
"connection has used a private profile route; a confirmed stop signals "
"shutdown even if its acknowledgement is lost. Thus transport readiness "
"and shutdown acceptance do not claim that profile work settled (server.py"
" (`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/server.py`), server.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/server.py`), server.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/server.py`), server.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/server.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/006-local-runtime-transport-worker-custody-and-lifecycle.md:22
msgid ""
"Each `ProfileWorkerProcess` represents one profile identity and is "
"launched inside the native process scope. Construction opens separate "
"custody and operation endpoints, starts an isolated worker, verifies its "
"native peer before the handshake, checks product/root/boot and worker "
"identity, then authenticates a second channel for operations. It "
"transfers the process only after both listeners are retired. No lease or "
"key is sent during construction. The custody channel manages API "
"preparation, lease install/refresh/share/retire, health, and human login;"
" the operation channel serializes private submissions, "
"start/observe/resume, result/review projection, per-page disclosure, "
"management, and secret delivery. Large submission payloads use "
"begin/chunk/finish/abort messages and do not become canonical admission "
"until upload completion. A runtime-owned authorization server supplies "
"lease authority; the worker is explicitly a custody transport, not an "
"independent admission authority. Health and cleanup preserve unresolved "
"resource owners; shutdown contains the process before waiting on "
"transport locks to avoid deadlocking an operation that needs the caller’s"
" profile guard (profile_worker.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/profile_worker.py`), "
"profile_worker.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/profile_worker.py`), "
"profile_worker.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/profile_worker.py`), "
"profile_worker.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/profile_worker.py`), "
"profile_worker.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/profile_worker.py`), "
"profile_worker.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/profile_worker.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/006-local-runtime-transport-worker-custody-and-lifecycle.md:24
msgid ""
"The operation-settlement helpers pin profile, session, and frontend at "
"submission, then require those identities and the exact operation "
"definition, subject, and contract on every observation. They return only "
"a canonical terminal projection, then read a result tied to that terminal"
" revision and contract digest. Higher-level clients use this flow for "
"profile fact mutations, modelo work-unit metadata reads/rename/discard, "
"and passphrase rotation. Mutation wrappers reject mismatched schemas and "
"result identities and preserve the operation ID plus only observed "
"terminal/effect facts on error, allowing recovery without claiming "
"rollback. Modelo mutations additionally require `UPDATED`. Passphrase "
"rotation sends current/new/confirmation values through the secret route, "
"clears mutable credential buffers, waits for the original operation to "
"settle, then requires a newly opened client authenticated with the "
"replacement password to read the exact successful result. It does not "
"retry the mutation itself (operation_settlement.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/operation_settlement.py`), "
"operation_settlement.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/operation_settlement.py`), "
"profile_mutations.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/profile_mutations.py`), "
"modelo_metadata.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/modelo_metadata.py`), "
"modelo_metadata.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/modelo_metadata.py`), "
"profile_password_rotation.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/profile_password_rotation.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/006-local-runtime-transport-worker-custody-and-lifecycle.md:26
msgid ""
"Manager adapters and shared service definitions keep provisioning "
"separate from profile authority. Fixed, absolute `systemctl`, `systemd-"
"run`, and `launchctl` executables run with bounded output, sanitized "
"locale/path, no stdin, and no captured stderr; a tool timeout does not "
"prove the manager rejected an already accepted action. Windows task XML, "
"macOS LaunchAgent plists, and Linux user units pin "
"executable/root/version and expose on-demand start separately from the "
"explicit login-autostart choice. The macOS adapter compares persisted "
"plist, effective ServiceManagement facts, and a bounded `launchctl print`"
" view before recognizing a binding. Configuration refuses to change "
"policy beneath a loaded job; stop checks the exact binding and watches "
"the retained process incarnation, but neither manager success nor process"
" exit proves domain settlement. The cross-platform installed binding "
"selects only the installed executable and does not search `PATH` or "
"provision during ordinary status/admission (manager_commands.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/manager_commands.py`), "
"service_definitions.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/service_definitions.py`), "
"macos_manager.py (`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/macos_manager.py`),"
" macos_manager.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/macos_manager.py`), "
"runtime_manager_composition.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/runtime_manager_composition.py`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/006-local-runtime-transport-worker-custody-and-lifecycle.md:28
msgid "Knowledge, security, and implementation assessment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/006-local-runtime-transport-worker-custody-and-lifecycle.md:30
msgid ""
"The chunk’s knowledge is operational identity and canonical application "
"state: owner/root identity, runtime boot and connection IDs, "
"profile/session leases, registered operation contracts, terminal "
"revisions, and native service/process observations. It does not supply "
"broad domain or legal reference material. Trust is layered across "
"filesystem/pipe/socket ownership, kernel peer identity, protocol "
"handshake, runtime authorization, and typed operation results. Important "
"positive controls include no-clobber or compare-before-publish "
"configuration, secret separation and mutable-buffer clearing, fixed "
"manager binaries, isolated worker startup, distinct custody/operation "
"channels, per-page result authority, bounded "
"deadlines/output/concurrency, and explicit unknown/uncertain results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/006-local-runtime-transport-worker-custody-and-lifecycle.md:32
msgid ""
"Some wrapper assurance is uneven. `run_profile_mutation` checks "
"successful terminal condition and requires a result revision at least as "
"large as the request’s expected revision, but does not itself require an "
"`UPDATED` effect; unlike modelo mutation and password rotation, it "
"returns the observed effect without asserting a particular value. Confirm"
" whether the registry/core contract supplies that guarantee before "
"callers treat this wrapper as proof of a committed change "
"(profile_mutations.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/profile_mutations.py`), "
"profile_mutations.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/profile_mutations.py`), "
"modelo_metadata.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/modelo_metadata.py`)). Secret "
"rotation clears mutable bytearrays, but its JSON encoding temporarily "
"creates immutable strings/bytes that Python cannot overwrite in place. "
"The Windows worker environment is inherited with only Python/loader-"
"related variable names filtered, whereas Linux uses a fixed environment; "
"if deployments place credentials in other environment variables, the "
"Windows child receives them (profile_password_rotation.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/profile_password_rotation.py`), "
"profile_worker.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/adapters/local_runtime/profile_worker.py`)). These are "
"concrete limits of the local implementations; whether they are "
"exploitable or violate product policy depends on adjacent composition and"
" deployment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/006-local-runtime-transport-worker-custody-and-lifecycle.md:34
msgid ""
"The transport server, worker, and manager code are careful about not "
"equating acknowledgement, configuration, process launch, process exit, "
"and application settlement. Remaining system boundaries include the "
"trustworthiness of kernel peer metadata, systemd/launchd/Task Scheduler "
"state, the profile-handler’s authorization decisions, and platform API "
"semantics under races. macOS process watches retain one process "
"incarnation and explicitly do not prove descendant containment. The "
"report’s chunk includes no tests; static review cannot certify real OS "
"API behavior, manager output parsing across OS versions, concurrent "
"filesystem attacks, or runtime session policy. Parent-level syntax and "
"import checks are not behavioral proof."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/006-local-runtime-transport-worker-custody-and-lifecycle.md:36
msgid "Dependencies and follow-up"
msgstr "Függőségek és további vizsgálatok"

#: ../../technical/articles/006-local-runtime-transport-worker-custody-and-lifecycle.md:38
msgid ""
"Synthesis should trace the server’s profile-handler calls into the "
"application authority, then connect worker lease and operation messages "
"to their canonical handlers and persistence. It should compare the native"
" endpoint identity reported here with the login evidence and worker-"
"containment adapters in adjacent chunks. It should also resolve whether "
"profile mutation contracts guarantee `UPDATED`, and whether Windows "
"deployments intentionally permit inherited non-loader environment values."
msgstr ""

